{%- comment -%}
  How many packs each delivery of a selling plan holds, so the shopper never
  runs out: for 30-day packs, 1 every 30 days, 2 every 60, 3 every 90; a
  90-day pack on the 90-day plan is 1. At least 1, and 1 when the plan doesn't
  say. The Liquid twin of supplyUnits in
  packages/shopify/src/subscribe-and-save.ts.

  Outputs a number; capture it, then `| plus: 0`.

  Accepts:
  - selling_plan: {Object} the plan (allocation.selling_plan)
  - pack_days: {Number} days (or servings) one unit holds; 30 when omitted
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign pack = pack_days | default: 30 | plus: 0
  capture days
    render 'plan-interval-days', selling_plan: selling_plan
  endcapture
  assign days = days | plus: 0
  assign units = 1
  if days > 0
    assign units = days | times: 1.0 | divided_by: pack | round
    if units < 1
      assign units = 1
    endif
  endif
  echo units
-%}
